      "key": "DeviceInfo",
      "kind": "singleton",
      "doc": {
        "summary": "Read-only description of the machine the process runs on.",
        "details": "DeviceInfo answers \"what is this machine\": its user-visible name, hardware model, and operating system. It deliberately excludes dynamic resource metrics (CPU load, memory) and any unique machine identifier. Values are read from the platform on every call; a getter whose value the platform cannot provide returns an empty string.\n\nTypical usage:\n\n```cpp\nauto& info = nativeapi::DeviceInfo::GetInstance();\nstd::string model = info.GetModel();  // e.g. \"MacBookPro18,1\"\n```"
      },
